 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "For powers of the same base:\nMultiplying: add the indices. a³ × a² = (a × a × a) × (a × a) = a⁵, so aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ.\nDividing: subtract the indices. a⁵ ÷ a² = a³, so aᵐ ÷ aⁿ = aᵐ⁻ⁿ.\nA power of a power: multiply the indices. (a²)³ = a² × a² × a² = a⁶, so (aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ.\nIndex zero: a³ ÷ a³ = a⁰, and any number divided by itself is 1, so a⁰ = 1 (a not 0).\nThe laws only work when the bases are the same: 2³ × 5² cannot be written as one power.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "m": 4,
   "n": 3,
   "k": 2
  },
  "problem": "Simplify {pw('x', m)} × {pw('x', n)} ÷ {pw('x', k)}, giving the answer as one power of x.",
  "steps": [
   "Multiplying: add the indices. {pw('x', m)} × {pw('x', n)} = {pw('x', m + n)}.",
   "Dividing: subtract the indices. {pw('x', m + n)} ÷ {pw('x', k)} = {pw('x', m + n - k)}."
  ],
  "answer": "{pw('x', m + n - k)}",
  "checks": [
   "m + n - k == 5"
  ]
 },
